Z||000006||grinthock||07-11-2001||08:41 PM||||Just played it, what a dissapointment....<P>The car models are flat, they didn't use guraurd shading, and the anti-aliasing is poor, there is tiling in alot of places and unjoined verticies, so you can see light through the side of buildings and cars.<P>The game was rushed.  <P>The menu interface STINKS, Before you selected the manufacturer then car, now you just scroll through a list of 30 cars (too long a list, and not enough cars now)<P>not as many car choices... On the back of the box it says "All the major manufacuteres"  But GM/Pontiac isn't listed.<P>I havn't had enough time to finish evaluating the game as I only played for 20 minutes on someone elses' system.  So far it's not impressive..<P>The most impressive part is the environment!  THE Environmental Bump Mapping and use of High bit textures makes the environemnt look great, and the lighting is well done, but poor in some areas, especially when a light source hits a vehicle!<P>The rally mode is VERY impressive the force feedback is very realistic, and the suspension feels great.  Turbo meter is cool (better than gt2)  It's a great mode, the most improvements yet<P>The use of heat mirage effects ruins the graphical effects in the replays.<P>Opening video was no fun.<P>My .02 I was gonna buy a PS2 JUST for that game -- Now I am going to wait a buy a gamecube<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||banditbalz||07-11-2001||10:28 PM||||I picked up my copy this afternoon. All we can say is  A W E S O M E !<P>Been playing it for the past 2 hours with a few other people and we just can't put the game down. It has a great soundtrack including Lenny Kravitz, Jimi Hendrix, The Cult and Motley Crew.<P>"The menu interface STINKS" <P>nobody here had a problem or a complaint!<P>"the anti-aliasing is poor" <P>uhmmm, I have a Intel Celeron 400, 128 mb ram, Voodooo 3DFX video card and I have never seen anti-aliasing half as smooth as this machine is capable of. <P>"All the major manufacuteres" But GM/Pontiac isn't listed.<P>actually, it says "All of the worlds TOP manufacturers"<P>"The game was rushed." <P>That's funny, it took them over 2 years to develope and bring it to market. <P>"Now I am going to wait a buy a gamecube"<P>have fun! beep, beep, beep, boing!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bannerfieroBeck_15.jpg"> <P>_www.geocities.com/banditbalz/<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||07-11-2001||10:34 PM||||Ohhhhh George lays the smack down.<P>Perhaps Pole Positionis more Grinthocks speed??<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||07-12-2001||01:46 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by banditbalz:<BR><B>uhmmm, I have a Intel Celeron 400, 128 mb ram, Voodooo 3DFX video card and I have never seen anti-aliasing half as smooth as this machine is capable of</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ummm.. unless you have a GeForce 2 or 3 you don't have any anti-aliasing on that comp   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>A T-Bird 1.2ghz and a Hercules 3d Prophet 4500 set at 4x FSAA.. now that's smooooth   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><FONT SIZE="1">edit:typo</FONT><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||TRiAD||07-12-2001||10:10 AM||||<B>W O W !</B><P>My only complaint...it's very difficult to get "simulation mode" going. You start with 18K, and only have like 3 cars you could afford. Races don't pay crap (so far) and everything is expensive. <P>But the licenses are WAY easier...<P>Final verdict (so far); I'm LOVING this game!||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierofreek2001||07-12-2001||11:49 AM||||tell em how it is banditbalz!!  gt3 is F#*$#( AWESOME LOOKIN!<BR>and i agree totally, the game was never rushed, i have been waiting for a long long time, it was originally supposed to come out when the system did<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg">   <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL><P>[This message has been edited by fierofreek2001 (edited 07-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fierofreek2001 (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||grinthock||07-12-2001||03:45 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>  ummm.. unless you have a GeForce 2 or 3 you don't have any anti-aliasing on that comp       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>A T-Bird 1.2ghz and a Hercules 3d Prophet 4500 set at 4x FSAA.. now that's smooooth       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><FONT SIZE="1">edit:typo</FONT><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That's correct!!!! Some people just do'nt understand I have a GeForce3 64MB DDR.. With a P4 1.7, and WOW... The FSAA is great... <P>Let's do some comparison....<P>----------XBOX--------PS2-------GameCube<P>CPU-------733P3-----Sony 300------IBM 405<BR>Graphics---250MHZ-GF3-150MHZ Sony--202MHZ ATI<BR>MEmory-----64MB---------32MB---------43MB<BR>Mem Bandwidth<BR>----------6.4GIG/S----3.2GIG/S----3.2G/s<BR>PolyGonPerf <BR>----------125M/S------66M/S---------??????<P>Fill Rate No Textures <BR>-----------4.0G/sec-AA---2.4G/sec------?????<P>Fill Rate W/Textures<BR>-----------4.0G/Sec-aa---1.2G/sec------?????<P>Full Screen<BR>Anti Alias<BR>-----------YES 6:1-----NO HARDWARE-----YES<P>Now looking at the results... Oh this info from <BR> <A HREF="http://www.httpcity.com/dnetwork/games/consoleb/mixdef.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.httpcity.com/dnetwork/games/consoleb/mixdef.html</A> <P>In case someone wants to see my information<P>The PS2 HAS NO ANTI ALIASING IN HARDWARE!  And we know that no FSAA Hardware support means that whenever you turn on FSAA the system slows to a SUPER HALT!  Because it can't handle all the work (FSAA is MAJOR cpu work!)  Now because of the failure of sony to add Hardware FSAA support the fill rates are CRAP, Xbox can maintain 4GIGpixels/sec FSAA while PS2 can do only 1.2GIG NON AA! With textures and we all know that W/Texutres is what COUNTS!  Let's add in the fact that the graphics card runs ALOT slower and the memory bandwidth is HALF!  That means we can't get thoes nice FSAA High Qual textures to the video memory FAST enough because there isn't enough mem bandwidth, this is easily seen at <A HREF="http://www.tomshardware.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tomshardware.com</A>  in his comparisions of videos cards, the tests he runs routinly hit memory bandwidth bottlenecks and the software out does the hardware which is what GT3 has done, it is TOO much for the PS2.<P>I could go on, but I wo'nt... Basically PS2 came out early....<P>Oh as for my comment about GT3 being rushed I didn't mena rushed I meant they didn't spend the time to do it right, so what the hell did they spend ALL the time developing anyway!?!? I have a close friend in the gaming industry who says that the only company REALLY seriously making games for PS2 is Sony because the system itself is terrible, everyone else is doing gamecube and xbox dev.  The PS2 hardware is crap and requires 5x the code to do the work because it ALL needs to be done in software (Such as the FSAA!)<P><BR>That's my fifty-five cents.<P>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||grinthock||07-12-2001||06:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Ohhhhh George lays the smack down.<P>Perhaps Pole Positionis more Grinthocks speed??<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually to respond to that --- I found the game unrealistically SLOW.  I have driven at 150MPH in a car and it was a HELL of a lot faster than GT3 shows it to be, there was an article in today's GLOBE AND MAIL and one Jack V -- Cart racer said the same thing.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||TRiAD||07-12-2001||08:01 PM||||I'll be the first to admit the technical stuff is WAY beyond me, but I've noticed mainly PC guys (and MAC at that) are the ones "gearing up" for the 'Cube. Sony has ALWAYS rules the console market, and the only way you're ever going to convince someone your stuff is better is to just shut up and make something better. (not directed towards anyone here). <P>Every racing game out there (Ridge racer comes to mind) claims to be "better the Gran Turismo", now these new system claim to be "better than PS2"...blah blah blah. <BR>make a better console with equal or better selection of games and equal or better support, and people will buy it. There's no need to advertise stuff that doesn't exist yet. <BR>If it's better when it comes out, than it'll be better. <P>The Camaro has outrun the Mustang since they were concieved, but the Mustang outsold it <B>4 to 1</B>, and now the F bodies are gone...I would presume the 'Cube will go the way of the Camaro. <P>That's my $.02.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||ray b||07-13-2001||01:40 AM||||how does gt3 compare to grand prix legends<BR>gpl is a real sim and is very hard to drive<BR>but is not a game more like a drivers school.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pontiaddict||07-13-2001||02:20 AM||||Played GT3 today.<BR>Man, if a Miata really handles like the one in the game, I'll never buy one.<P>Since it's my friends game he picked a Pt. Cruiser as the first car.<BR>It's now got about 245 turbocharged horses and I was outrunning Vipers, Camaros and Z06 Corvettes earlier tonight with it. (couldn't beat the Cobra though.)<BR>[I don't know why ricers think that a few simple mods will make their real car do the same.]<BR>The replay menu after each race got old quick.<BR>And while the daytime graphics looked decent, Sony should be banned from making driving games take place at night. At least with GT3 they actually put headligts that actually cast light from them on the cars, not that they really help.<P>Maybe Microsoft should just use ported PS1 games badged as Xbox games for their first linup. That's what Sony did for the PS2 when it first came out. I guess they wouldn't have to port them, since the PS1 games are backwards compatable, but they still had to make them not work on Playstations.||||reg||1
Z||000017||fierobaby||07-13-2001||02:58 AM||||ok I have to agree with everyone here...its an alright game...I'm not much for the racing but hey whatever...I actully like GT2 better but only cause I have a thing for that Gabage song.... I dunno I havn't decided wheather to like it or hate it ....we'll see<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> AIM: Fierobaby87<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000018||artherd||07-13-2001||06:23 AM||||Hi Ray, I just hav eto say;<BR>I LOVE GRAND PRIX LEGENDS!!!!<P>Woah, woah WOOOAHAAAAAHHHH!!! :)<P>Bloody great, hook it to surround sound, get a steering wheel and pedal set for the computer, and use a video projector for the screen, and HOLD ON TIGHT! ;)<P>IT's the first, and only, computer game I've ever played that I would even call realistic.<P>Man, that Lotous can oversteer when they tyres are cold!   I gotta love the wail of the Ferrari's V12 though.  It's also a faster car (for me at least :)<P>Best!!!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
